From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jokubas Maciulaitis <ubitas52@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 22:58:53 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] mtd: ubi: count the fastmap blocks attaching by fastmap did
 not scan

A fastmap that does not fit into one PEB has data blocks that can be
anywhere, but attaching by fastmap scans only the first
UBI_FM_MAX_START PEBs and so finds just the anchor and whatever else is
there. ubi_wl_init() counts the fastmap PEBs from that list, comes up
short of good_peb_count by the data blocks it missed, and fails its
assertion with a stack dump on every attach, here with 16 KiB PEBs and
a four block fastmap. Count the current fastmap blocks that were not in
the list too.
---
 drivers/mtd/ubi/wl.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mtd/ubi/wl.c b/drivers/mtd/ubi/wl.c
index fefcbaf..b24d716 100644
--- a/drivers/mtd/ubi/wl.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/ubi/wl.c
@@ -1801,7 +1801,7 @@ out_free:
  */
 int ubi_wl_init(struct ubi_device *ubi, struct ubi_attach_info *ai)
 {
-	int err, i, reserved_pebs, found_pebs = 0;
+	int err, i, reserved_pebs, found_pebs = 0, fm_pebs = 0;
 	struct rb_node *rb1, *rb2;
 	struct ubi_ainf_volume *av;
 	struct ubi_ainf_peb *aeb, *tmp;
@@ -1893,6 +1893,7 @@ int ubi_wl_init(struct ubi_device *ubi, struct ubi_attach_info *ai)
 		if (e) {
 			ubi_assert(!ubi->lookuptbl[e->pnum]);
 			ubi->lookuptbl[e->pnum] = e;
+			fm_pebs++;
 		} else {
 			bool sync = false;
 
@@ -1925,6 +1926,14 @@ int ubi_wl_init(struct ubi_device *ubi, struct ubi_attach_info *ai)
 		found_pebs++;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Attaching by fastmap only scans the first UBI_FM_MAX_START PEBs, so
+	 * the fastmap's data blocks after them are not in @ai->fastmap. They
+	 * are in use all the same.
+	 */
+	if (ubi->fm)
+		found_pebs += ubi->fm->used_blocks - fm_pebs;
+
 	dbg_wl("found %i PEBs", found_pebs);
 
 	ubi_assert(ubi->good_peb_count == found_pebs);
